hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1715","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from his father Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr who said: al-Harith ibn Khazamah came with these two verses from the end of Baraah, There has come to you a Messenger from among yourselves, to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: Who is with you for this? He said: I do not know, by Allah, except that I bear witness that I heard them from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and comprehended and memorized them. Umar said: And I bear witness that I heard them from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then he said: Had they been three verses I would have made them a separate surah. Look to a surah of the Quran and place them in it, so they placed them at the end of Baraah."
